{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And it is dim.</b> The question is: why does it say <b>and it is dim</b>, since it is speaking of the initial inspection? And one may answer: <b>and it is not</b> — this is what it says, like 'the hope of the lowly shall perish forever.' And similarly the meaning of 'and it is depressed, it is not of the skin and it is not dim' — but if it is dim, it is obvious that it is pure." "<b>והיא כהה</b> Written with a yod."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The abbreviation חז״ק appears to introduce a difficulty; rendered as 'the question is.' The word א before איננה in the MS seems to introduce the answer י״מ, left untranslated as it appears to be a formatting marker. The 'and it is not' reading understands איננה as the key word being expounded."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:53.930064589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}